      "content": "To capture local risk better, consider incorporating geospatial indicators such as average building age or the density of commercial activity within a small radius. Another useful proxy is the proximity to known high-risk features, like flood zones, historical fire corridors, or areas with high concentrations of specific building materials. Additionally, variables reflecting urban canopy cover can serve as a strong environmental predictor for various perils. These neighborhood-level features should help your model capture subtle, hyperlocal risk variations missed by broad demographic or financial data.",
