      "content": "While demographic shifts are statistically correlated with risk, ethically and practically, race or ethnicity are often prohibited features in insurance modeling due to regulatory constraints and bias concerns. Instead of direct demographic identifiers, focus on highly granular, non-protected proxies for economic stress or social capital, which are far more defensible. For example, use measures like Median Household Income variance or unemployment rates at the census tract level, as these capture the economic environment linked to certain populations without violating equitable modeling principles. These metrics statistically capture the socioeconomic conditions you are observing.",
